WEBVTT

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.270
See you later, Riou.

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:07.650
Okay.

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:13.150
I'm hungry. Take was way too spirited.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.950
I'm home.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.870
Hey, loser.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:24.870
Brother, you're back?

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.420
I came to get my laundry, loser.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:29.460
Hey...

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:30.920
What is it, loser?

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:33.550
Stop calling me that. Everyone tried-

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:37.350
Don't say something so spoiled.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:40.640
That spirit of yours is the reason why you weren't invited to Bijou.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.640
If someone like you is a
candidate for the regulars,

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:44.600
then Tousei will lose in the first round next year as well!

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.240
Feeling frustrated, Riou?

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:56.110
Good.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:00.870
I will get revenge with everyone from Bijou.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.790
So bring <i>all</i> of your data for the game with Nishiura.

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:08.210
After that, get in touch with Tajima...

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:10.710
and drop him into a trap or something.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:48.730
Chiyo.

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:51.520
Hey, good work.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:53.520
Hey, I lost.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:57.280
We want to ask you something, but... is now okay?

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:58.570
Sure.

00:02:58.570 --> 00:02:59.990
You can go ahead.

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:01.070
Okay.

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:02.410
Sorry. Is it okay?

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:03.870
It's absolutely fine.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:04.450
What is it?

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:07.120
Well...

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:09.790
Are you good friends with the cheering squad leader?

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.330
Hamada?

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:14.170
Well, I've talked to him.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:15.500
Well...

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:16.550
Um...

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:18.090
Well...

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.010
S-Say...

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:24.600
...if we were to become cheer girls...

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.720
Cheer girls? In the cheering squad?

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:29.060
Awesome-

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:29.520
Wait!

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:30.730
Don't be hasty!

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:31.310
Huh?

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:35.730
Well, we're in the dance club.

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:37.150
Oh, that's right.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:40.740
Which one? There are about three dance clubs, right?

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:43.070
Isn't it the one with a model as a member?

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:44.990
The really pretty person!

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:47.740
Ochi is really pretty!

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:49.830
Even looking at her every day doesn't get tiring.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:51.540
But that person...

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:52.420
might not do it.

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:53.960
Or more like she won't do it.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:56.210
Models don't go out under the sun.

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:57.420
That's not it.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:58.880
The second and third years won't come.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:00.340
Is that so?

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:04.890
We dance jazz and hip-hop, and they said it's completely different from cheering.

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:06.890
The miniskirt and pom-poms are different too.

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:09.350
They also don't know anyone in the baseball club.

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:10.680
I got it.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:12.980
In other words, you two want to do it, but...

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:15.900
it'd be troublesome if people thought that the entire dance club was willing to do it.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.360
That's right.

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:19.900
Would it be okay with just the two of us?

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.780
Or would it be better if we just give it up?

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:24.110
I like cheer girls.

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:26.200
I think that everyone will like it too.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.280
Shinooka.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:30.830
Starting today, I'm going to have Mihashi eat three rice balls, so...

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.790
can you make one more?

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:34.460
Yeah, sure.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:36.130
Just for Mihashi?

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:39.880
Yeah. He's lost weight, so I'm making him eat rice.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.590
Any kind of filling will do.

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:42.300
Okay.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:43.670
Please take care of it.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:46.800
Later.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.060
You talked to them! You talked!

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:50.060
Well, of course.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:51.890
One more rice ball.

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:53.020
My, how close.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:53.230
It's communication about duties!
My, how close.

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:54.140
"Please take care of it."
It's communication about duties!

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:54.810
"Later."
It's communication about duties!

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:57.690
Chiyo, are you going out with anyone?

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:00.270
There isn't even a bit of that kind of atmosphere.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:03.240
Could it be that you two are aiming for Hamada?

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:04.030
No.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:05.240
We just want to dance.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:05.950
Really?

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:06.820
Yeah.

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:11.990
Got it, Mihashi?

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:17.290
You're going to run beside me,
staying three meters away at all times.

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:19.920
O-Okay.

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:22.960
Here we go!

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:23.800
All right.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:27.050
Tajima ran!

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:32.970
L-Like this.

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:46.360
What is Mihashi doing on his own?

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:46.900
Stop him!

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:47.450
Ootsuka!
Stop him!

00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:48.530
Okay!

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:51.660
Kojima!

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.330
I can't get through.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:54.410
Tajima!

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:58.500
Three meters.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:00.130
Mihashi!

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:02.670
All right! It bounced up!

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:03.300
Go!

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:06.510
All right!

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:07.300
Goal.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.760
Tajima is like a superstar.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:12.100
Are you okay?

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:14.390
That was a huge success, Mihashi!

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:17.350
Tajima is... amazing.

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:18.310
We're going to score one more goal.

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:19.900
I'm counting on you, three meters.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:21.770
Y-Yeah!

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:22.980
Let's go!

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:24.070
Yeah!

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:27.740
Having an older brother, I could cry, Mihashi...

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:30.820
It looks good!

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:32.740
Let's eat!

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:36.790
But really, Tajima can do anything, huh?

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.620
I play soccer a lot during winter.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.540
I see. During the off-season, huh?

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:43.750
I often played soccer in middle school.

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:46.300
It's no good! There are other people here as well.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:47.590
Then should I call him over?

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:48.550
Shinooka!

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:52.470
What's wrong?

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:54.470
It's nothing.

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:55.890
I'll see you later.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:56.430
Sure.

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:56.930
Geez.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:59.890
There were two girls behind her, right?

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:00.690
Ah, really?

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:02.100
You know...

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:05.610
If you win one or two more times, you might get interviews for the newspaper.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:07.860
Is that so?

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:11.410
With only ten first years, you defeated Tousei.

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:13.070
I think that alone would make a story.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:17.580
Since there are still a lot of schools left, the reporters are scattered.

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:21.420
But if you win two more games, you'd be in the best 16, right? You might get the attention, then.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:24.130
I wonder who they'll show for the pictures.

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:26.210
Maybe me? Maybe Mihashi?

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:27.630
Wouldn't it normally be Hanai?

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:29.800
No, it'd be the coach, wouldn't it?

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:31.130
Coach?

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:34.180
If I were a reporter, I'd ask,
"Just who are you?"

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:35.550
Actually, I wish someone would ask her.

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:37.810
Where did she polish up those fungoes?

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:40.100
Aren't you curious?

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:41.270
Like about her age?

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:43.700
Then how about her first name?

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:44.230
Momoe!

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.980
That's her last name, isn't it? That's not what I mean.

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:49.070
What time are we supposed to meet up to go see the game?

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:50.150
One o'clock at the back gate.

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:52.450
We need to change clothes, so I guess we should wake up at 12:50 pm.

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:53.910
What time is it now?

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:54.950
It's 12:10 pm.

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:57.620
Am I the weird one?

00:07:57.620 --> 00:07:58.950
Coach "Momo" Momoe!

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:00.870
Thanks for the meal! Good night!

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:04.830
Good night.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:09.170
Other than age, they don't talk about cup size or something?

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:16.350
Ah, I see. That's why the conversation ended.

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:22.430
Well, I wouldn't want the newspaper or whatever to treat the coach in such a way either.

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:23.810
Sorry.

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:32.530
Hey, Roka.

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:36.240
Are you depressed, ex-captain?

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:39.580
Yes, I'm depressed.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.620
As much as you were two years ago.

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:46.960
You've gotten bolder, Kazuki.

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:49.130
Well, have a seat.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:50.300
What'll you have?

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:51.590
You can have anything.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:53.630
Up to 1500 yen, that is.

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:59.970
Then dumplings for 185 yen, shark fin rice for 811 yen
and Torufan fried chicken for 504 yen.

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:06.100
You have some strange skills. It's exactly 1500 yen.

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:08.310
I'll answer each question in 100 yen increments.

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:10.940
You better speak 1500 yen's worth.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:14.900
I think 1500 yen is good up until the third inning of the last game.

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:18.070
You... really get what you want, don't you?

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:19.450
I'll accept a supplement.

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:21.240
I can't put out any more money.

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:24.790
Even if you didn't call me,
Riou would talk for free, right?

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:27.710
He didn't play in the game, so he's no good at all.

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:29.130
How about the video?

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:32.000
You made him take it out along with the data, right?

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:34.420
Bijou doesn't have a video group?

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:35.010
We do.

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:35.880
Can I take your order?

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:39.930
Dumplings, shark fin rice and Torufan fried chicken.

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:40.300
Very well.

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:42.010
Thanks for the food.
Very well.

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:45.850
Normally, we have the parents' association take turns to film, but...

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:48.020
this time both matches were on the same day.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:52.860
The parents of the third years and bench-warmers watched their children's game.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:56.610
So the parents of the first years followed the ball while filming for the first time.

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:58.160
How nostalgic.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:01.370
My parents did that too, thinking it was a good thing.

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:02.830
I can't laugh.

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:05.580
We entrusted them to do this, so it's a real setback.

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:08.420
Did you guys...

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:11.960
lose by a mere fluke or by self-destruction?

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:16.010
There was that too.

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:19.840
But I don't think it was just that.

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:27.560
If I were to put it bluntly, I thought that we'd have it easy until the fifth round.

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:31.900
Then a dark horse suddenly appeared. No wonder you're unsettled.

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:37.740
When I thought that your team noticed Nishiura's weirdness due to our loss,

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:40.110
I felt a little vexed, so I poked fun at you.

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:41.410
Sorry.

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:44.410
Did you not want to talk about it?

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:46.080
That's not it.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:48.410
I want to pay you back for taking care of me and all.

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:51.210
It's good that I did you some favors.

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:53.670
I'm glad you have that kind of personality.

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:57.550
You sure don't mince your words even though I'm replying seriously.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:59.050
About that...

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:00.930
I saw the video too, but...

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:03.510
you guys were horrible.

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:05.430
Ah, that's right.

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:08.020
At the beginning, were you aiming for a curveball?

00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:11.060
Because up until the middle innings,
the pitches centered around curveballs.

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:15.230
But in the last half, they switched to fastballs.

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:17.360
Were all those hit upwards?

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:17.980
Yes.

00:11:17.980 --> 00:11:19.690
What kind of pitch was it?

00:11:19.690 --> 00:11:21.700
I thought of various things, but...

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:24.950
I can't say it's anything other than a habit of his to throw the ball.

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:27.660
The rotation wasn't clean.

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:30.710
I thought it was slow but faster than I expected.

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:34.170
Or more like it passed higher than the expected trajectory.

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:36.670
His form might've been a deception too.

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:40.590
Were they purposely using that habitual pitch?

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:42.590
Of course.

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:45.550
It doesn't have any speed, so it's over once you get used to it.

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:49.100
That's why they were saving it in the first half, right?

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:51.690
How do you think one can hit it?

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:55.190
It'll be immediate if you get that guy to be your batting pitcher.

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:58.360
In other words, there's no way to practice for it.

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:02.950
Hey, let me have a bite.

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:04.200
No.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:08.290
Doesn't it bother you that I only have water?

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:09.120
Not at all.

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:11.000
Then next is base stealing.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:12.370
What's with these numbers?

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:14.420
You didn't hear it from Riou?

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:16.790
I did. Was it Junta?

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:19.550
Even though you made a pick-off throw, you got bases stolen?

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:21.510
Tousei's using that kind of clumsy pitcher?

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:22.880
He's not clumsy.

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:27.300
From what the coach said, only number four could see the difference.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:29.220
Tajima Yuuichirou, huh?

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:32.390
What about the coach? It's a woman, right?

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:36.190
The thing is, she's got a good grasp of the players.

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:38.690
She puts out so many signs to the point of being annoying.

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:41.110
The variety of their signs might rival ours.

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:45.110
Seriously? When I was a first year, I couldn't remember all the signs.

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:48.120
The coach is young, right?

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:51.200
She's young... I think.

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:52.950
She's also pretty cute.

00:12:52.950 --> 00:12:54.120
And like this...

00:12:58.000 --> 00:12:59.420
"And like this..."?

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:04.760
Well, it's fine. You'll understand once you see her.

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:07.470
What about the defense?

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:10.510
We had a lot of fly balls,
so it's still unknown.

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:12.020
Oh, the right outfielder has a good arm.

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:14.180
The throw back home in the ninth inning?

00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:16.560
It was filmed in the useless video, so I saw it.

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:19.690
That was a big one.

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:27.070
How about the catcher?

00:13:27.070 --> 00:13:28.990
He has a normal arm.

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:30.990
If you consider that he's a first year, then it's on the strong side.

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:34.160
This guy also puts out incredibly detailed signs.

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:35.710
He's got a big variety of pitches.

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:37.420
As for walks and dead balls...

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:39.330
One, huh? His control's good.

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:43.460
Takashima said that his mitt doesn't move while he's catching.

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:46.680
Takashima? Was he on the bench?

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:50.010
The catcher's leads made the pitches vary a lot while keeping the same course.

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:52.850
Incredibly enough, they finished cleanly.

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:55.890
But the most surprising thing was the batting.

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:59.230
Almost everyone was able to follow the fastballs and sliders.

00:13:59.600 --> 00:14:02.230
In the end, number four was also able to hit a sinker.

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:06.860
I don't care why they lost.

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:10.200
Okay, so the strength of their defense is unknown.

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:13.370
Their batting probably matched up to Tousei.

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:15.750
When you win and advance in the spring,

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:18.370
it's such a pain because the opponent prepares for you like this.

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:22.340
Speaking of that, we have ten days for arranged practice.

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:24.750
It won't always stay this well for them, will it?

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:29.090
All that's left is to figure out how to score.

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:32.600
I'm done!

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:34.350
Thanks for the food! Later.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:35.930
Wait a sec!

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:39.560
What? I already finished eating.

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:40.730
Just this last thing.

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:44.730
If you were to do it one more time, where would you attack?

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:49.740
I would probably think the same way as you, Roka.

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:53.580
You're really putting on airs.

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:55.200
Well, whatever.

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:57.000
Well then, let's go.

00:14:58.250 --> 00:15:00.290
Thank you. It was delicious!

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:02.290
I'm hungry.

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:04.630
I'll hurry back and make dinner.

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:07.420
Huh? Aren't you in training camp?

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:10.930
I am in training camp. I'm making the dinner.

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:12.840
You are?

00:15:13.340 --> 00:15:15.430
The mothers come too.

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:19.020
When it's for 50 people, it becomes hard labor, you know.

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:22.350
Is the coach doing well?

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:24.980
Takii? He's energetic.

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:26.270
Idiotically energetic.

00:15:26.270 --> 00:15:27.900
Or more like he's an idiot.

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:31.650
He can't throw anymore, but he's always energetic.

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:36.990
If I remember right, Takii broke his shoulder in the third year of middle school.

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:39.620
He went to Bijou instead of Tousei for high school too.

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:44.130
How was he able to return to baseball?

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:46.630
Kazuki.

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:50.210
Even though you lost in the first round,

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:55.550
your coach can still get you into a good college since you were the captain, right?

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:57.760
What's with those reference books?

00:15:58.260 --> 00:15:59.890
Aren't you going for a baseball recommendation?

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:03.190
It's better to have more choices.

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:06.230
Are you good at studying?

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:08.190
In the club, I'm probably the best at it.

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:10.860
The baseball club is full of idiots, isn't it?

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:12.860
That's nothing to be proud of at all.

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:13.990
Riou too...

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:15.870
He said he'll take the Bijou entrance exam normally.

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:18.790
I mean, have you ever seen his report card?

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:19.700
It's shameful, so I made him quit.

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:20.500
This is...

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:22.660
probably what bothered Riou.

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:27.710
I understand about Takii, but you...

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:32.880
Are you all right giving up playing?

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:33.880
Me?

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:37.220
I've had enough of running.

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:39.930
Being the coach is nice and easy.

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:40.640
Is that so?

00:16:41.970 --> 00:16:45.940
Among this year's third years, there are probably guys who'll quit baseball with this.

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:51.150
Then for years, they won't be able to watch high school baseball relays.

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:54.280
They'd change the channel when the sports news comes on.

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:56.910
Roka...

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:59.530
You're hurting my feelings, you know.

00:17:00.280 --> 00:17:01.950
I'm relieved.

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:04.460
It'd be pitiful if we were the only ones to have lost in the first round.

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:09.540
But if Tousei goes to Koshien next year, the people would be surprised, you know.

00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:11.090
That's true.

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:14.010
Riou's generation will then lose in the first round.

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:14.880
Funny!

00:17:18.340 --> 00:17:21.850
I can't tell how much of it was a joke with him.

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:30.230
Even if he jokes his way out of it, I can't forget the Roka from last summer.

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:47.540
While everyone was crying, Roka just stood there.

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:52.420
After the farewell ceremony, the third years stood on the field with tears on their faces.

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:55.420
However, Roka never came even once.

00:17:57.050 --> 00:18:00.890
And yet he is this involved with baseball again.

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:04.520
I wonder if I too...

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:15.320
will be able to feel like playing baseball again.

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:27.000
There sure are a lot of people for a weekday.

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:29.750
There are a lot behind the back net.

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:32.000
Shall we go watch from the seats by the infield near third base?

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:32.960
Okay!

00:18:33.380 --> 00:18:34.340
Now then.

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:38.800
As everyone knows, Tajima's right hand will take one week to completely heal.

00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:41.510
Therefore, he won't be in time for the third round,

00:18:41.510 --> 00:18:45.140
which is against the winner of this match.

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:49.520
In the third round, we'll remove Tajima from being the fourth batter and third baseman.

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:53.440
I'm fine! I'm fine!

00:18:55.440 --> 00:18:58.400
Injured people shouldn't complain to adults!

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:01.200
Will you all gather around for a bit?

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:03.620
I'm going to announce the third round's starting lineup.

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:05.790
Everyone, watch the game with this in mind.

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:06.700
Yes!

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:09.210
Number one. First baseman.

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:10.290
Tajima.

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:13.670
Yes.

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:17.550
There will be more left-handed batters, so you'll get strong hits at first base.

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:21.720
It's also very important for a fly ball pitcher like Mihashi.

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:27.310
No matter what you say, the first batter stands at the plate the most.

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:32.190
Also, the difficulty of stealing a base while having your feet watched is fun!

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:34.980
Number one. First baseman.

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:35.940
Tajima!

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:36.570
Yes!

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:37.530
She's good.

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:38.820
She's too good.

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:41.070
Number two. Second baseman.

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:42.700
Sakaeguchi.

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:43.700
Yes!

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:46.950
It's okay to think that my position didn't change because I was thought of well, right?

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:48.370
Number three. Third baseman.

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:49.540
Izumi.

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:50.370
Yes!

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:51.540
I'm the third batter!

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:52.830
Number four. Center fielder.

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:54.040
Hanai.

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:55.040
Yes!

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:57.040
Whoa, fourth batter.

00:19:57.460 --> 00:19:58.920
Put up some points for us.

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:00.340
Yes!

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:01.510
Number five. Shortstop.

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:02.680
Suyama.

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:03.590
Yes!

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:05.010
Number six. Catcher.

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:05.930
Abe.

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:06.800
Yes!

00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:09.850
I have to be as careful with my leads as in the Tousei game.

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:11.020
Number seven. Right fielder.

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:11.930
Oki.

00:20:11.930 --> 00:20:12.940
Yes!

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:14.900
The right fielder after Hanai, huh?

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:16.270
Number eight. Left fielder.

00:20:16.270 --> 00:20:17.190
Mizutani.

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:17.900
Yes!

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:20.440
Abe's spot. I dropped in the batting order.

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:21.900
Number nine. Pitcher.

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:22.780
Mihashi.

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:24.910
Yes!

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:26.030
That's it!

00:20:26.030 --> 00:20:29.660
For both batting and pitching, think about your own role while watching!

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:30.330
Yes!

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:33.790
First on offense is Iwatsuki West High School.

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:36.580
It's a school that gathers more than 60 members every year.

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:38.710
Last spring, they made it to the first round of the regionals,

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:41.630
and they advanced to the third round last summer.

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:44.430
It's a team that's established their strength these past ten years.

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:48.300
First on defense, Sakitama High School has ten members.

00:20:48.300 --> 00:20:52.430
With just one third year among them, it's a team centered around first and second years.

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:55.230
They didn't participate last spring because they didn't have enough members.

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:58.980
Last summer, they also got knocked out in the first round.

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:01.860
Hearing just this much, it seems that Iwatsuki West is stronger, but...

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:04.990
this game is Iwatsuki West's first for the summer.

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:05.860
Ah, I know!

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:09.330
I watched the high school baseball news at Mihashi's house.

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:12.540
The first round was a really close contest for Sakitama.

00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:20.670
In the end, it was 9 to 8.

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:22.550
He's right!

00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:23.710
Huh?

00:21:23.710 --> 00:21:25.090
Isn't that amazing?

00:21:25.090 --> 00:21:25.930
Well...

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:27.050
It's amazing.

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:29.260
That is, <i>you</i> are amazing for remembering that score.

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:32.100
It's because they're our opponent.

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:33.810
What? Over something so small?

00:21:33.810 --> 00:21:35.520
Can't he use that for other things?

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:37.730
Hanai, Tajima is amazing!

00:21:37.730 --> 00:21:41.320
Why the difference? Even though I saw the news twice...

00:21:41.820 --> 00:21:43.320
Well, that's how it is.

00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:46.280
Iwatsuki West's ability is probably higher, but...

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:49.820
Sakitama still has the momentum left from the previous game.

00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:51.950
Which team do you think will win?

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:53.910
I wonder which one.

00:21:57.250 --> 00:21:59.790
I have to watch carefully.

00:21:59.790 --> 00:22:03.170
I need them to let me pitch next time as well.

00:22:07.590 --> 00:22:10.760
Whichever team wins will be our next opponent.

00:23:42.140 --> 00:23:45.610
Having come to watch the game of our third round opponent,

00:23:45.610 --> 00:23:48.440
we were unintentionally overwhelmed by Sakitama High's catcher...

00:23:48.940 --> 00:23:53.700
and the awesome play of Sakura, the number five first year, during the game.

00:23:53.700 --> 00:23:56.160
I can't contain my excitement either.

00:23:56.160 --> 00:24:00.580
In the next game, how will the Nishiura nine challenge the third round opponent?

00:24:00.580 --> 00:24:04.790
In the middle of the strategy meeting,
an unthinkable revelation from Abe...

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:06.840
Next time:

00:24:06.840 --> 00:24:08.210
Sakitama.

00:24:08.210 --> 00:24:10.010
Abe is scary.
